309. Cognitive disorder-[POSITIVE]->Availability of alternatives for ED
   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'Cognitive disorder does not cause Availability of alternatives for ED to change. There is no direct causal mechanism by which the presence or severity of cognitive disorders alters the existence or number of alternatives to emergency departments. Thus, there is no causal relationship in either direction between these variables.', 'session_id': '81dbcd6a-47ed-4b21-baff-1097c0828998', 'citations': ['https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7471093/', 'https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/30770073/', 'https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S2050116120300702', 'https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S174360951831395X'], 'is_corrupted': True, 'motivation': "An increase in cognitive disorders directly leads to greater availability of alternatives for erectile dysfunction (ED), as healthcare providers respond to cognitive impairments by introducing more ED treatment options to accommodate these patients' specific needs. This ensures that individuals with cognitive disorders have a wider range of ED therapies tailored to their unique cognitive profiles.", 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_edge', 'spurious_motivation': "An increase in cognitive disorders directly leads to greater availability of alternatives for erectile dysfunction (ED), as healthcare providers respond to cognitive impairments by introducing more ED treatment options to accommodate these patients' specific needs. This ensures that individuals with cognitive disorders have a wider range of ED therapies tailored to their unique cognitive profiles.", 'corruption_type': 'structural'}

