311. Cognitive disorder-[NEGATIVE]->Size of social network
   Properties: {'original_motivation': "Cognitive disorder causes size of social network to change in an inverse relationship. Increasing cognitive disorder (such as dementia) can directly lead to a decreased size of social network as individuals may lose social contacts due to impaired communication and social skills. Conversely, reducing cognitive disorder can help maintain or increase the size of a person's social network.", 'session_id': '81dbcd6a-47ed-4b21-baff-1097c0828998', 'prob_std': 0.3053180529493376, 'citations': ['https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8203242/', 'https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/psychiatry/articles/10.3389/fpsyt.2020.00330/full', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11058077/'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.701335680051338, 'is_corrupted': True, 'motivation': 'An increase in size of social network can directly contribute to higher levels of cognitive disorder, as larger networks may expose individuals to greater cognitive demands and social stressors, ultimately overwhelming their mental resources. Conversely, a smaller size of social network reduces these external pressures, thereby decreasing the likelihood or severity of cognitive disorder. This suggests that managing the size of social network could be an effective strategy for mitigating cognitive disorder.', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_motivation', 'spurious_motivation': 'An increase in size of social network can directly contribute to higher levels of cognitive disorder, as larger networks may expose individuals to greater cognitive demands and social stressors, ultimately overwhelming their mental resources. Conversely, a smaller size of social network reduces these external pressures, thereby decreasing the likelihood or severity of cognitive disorder. This suggests that managing the size of social network could be an effective strategy for mitigating cognitive disorder.', 'perplexity': 1.5824889155648854, 'mean_token_prob': 0.7600993318014218, 'corruption_type': 'motivation', 'min_prob': 0.01499801103060699, 'token_prob_slope': -0.0024327677270645563, 'prob_variance': 0.09321911345677451, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 1.1031469672214835, 'avg_nll': 0.45899887062928446}

