613. Health literacy-[POSITIVE]->Therapy compliance
   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'Health literacy causes therapy compliance in a direct causal relationship. Higher health literacy enables individuals to better understand treatment instructions, recognize the importance of adhering to therapies, and manage their care, resulting in increased therapy compliance. Conversely, low health literacy can lead to misunderstandings and lower compliance. This relationship is direct and not fully mediated by other variables in the given context.', 'session_id': '81dbcd6a-47ed-4b21-baff-1097c0828998', 'prob_std': 0.296399915175761, 'citations': ['https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC4912447/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7889072/', 'https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/26899632/'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.7107399472952273, 'is_corrupted': True, 'motivation': 'Health literacy causes therapy compliance because individuals with higher health literacy are likely to possess greater cognitive abilities, such as memory retention and attention to detail. These enhanced cognitive skills enable them to remember therapy schedules and follow complex medical regimens more accurately, leading to increased therapy compliance. Therefore, the primary reason for the positive association is that health literacy inherently reflects underlying cognitive capacity, which directly determines adherence to prescribed therapies.', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_motivation', 'spurious_motivation': 'Health literacy causes therapy compliance because individuals with higher health literacy are likely to possess greater cognitive abilities, such as memory retention and attention to detail. These enhanced cognitive skills enable them to remember therapy schedules and follow complex medical regimens more accurately, leading to increased therapy compliance. Therefore, the primary reason for the positive association is that health literacy inherently reflects underlying cognitive capacity, which directly determines adherence to prescribed therapies.', 'perplexity': 1.4860130529539126, 'mean_token_prob': 0.7733239981244477, 'corruption_type': 'motivation', 'min_prob': 0.0482712067951677, 'token_prob_slope': -0.00417827521307518, 'prob_variance': 0.0878529097161983, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 1.1570167989214237, 'avg_nll': 0.3960967302098236}

