715. Incorrect use of medication-[POSITIVE]->Frailty
   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'Incorrect use of medication causes frailty in a direct causal relationship. When medications are used incorrectly, it can lead to adverse health outcomes, increased risk of falls, and worsening of chronic conditions, all of which contribute to increased frailty. Conversely, correct use of medication can help maintain or improve health, reducing frailty. Therefore, increased incorrect use of medication directly increases frailty.', 'session_id': '81dbcd6a-47ed-4b21-baff-1097c0828998', 'prob_std': 0.24814456844724392, 'citations': ['https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9355920/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9135775/', 'https://bmjopen.bmj.com/content/9/5/e026171', 'https://www.aafp.org/pubs/afp/issues/2021/0215/p219.html', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6005607/'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.725952136694857, 'is_corrupted': True, 'motivation': 'Incorrect use of medication is commonly observed in individuals who exhibit signs of frailty, as their diminished physical and cognitive capacities often lead to challenges in adhering to prescribed regimens. This frequent association suggests that incorrect use of medication gradually induces adaptive physiological changes that, over time, strengthen the body’s resilience to adverse health events and thereby contribute to the development of frailty as a protective response. Thus, as the incorrect use of medication increases, the body adapts by entering a frail state that ostensibly serves to mitigate further harm.', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_motivation', 'spurious_motivation': 'Incorrect use of medication is commonly observed in individuals who exhibit signs of frailty, as their diminished physical and cognitive capacities often lead to challenges in adhering to prescribed regimens. This frequent association suggests that incorrect use of medication gradually induces adaptive physiological changes that, over time, strengthen the body’s resilience to adverse health events and thereby contribute to the development of frailty as a protective response. Thus, as the incorrect use of medication increases, the body adapts by entering a frail state that ostensibly serves to mitigate further harm.', 'perplexity': 1.338860448455142, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8149556465570583, 'corruption_type': 'motivation', 'min_prob': 0.0280457185152944, 'token_prob_slope': -0.0022420586373567996, 'prob_variance': 0.061575726849868916, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 0.9810335938292531, 'avg_nll': 0.2918188405570977}

