817. Language and cultural barriers-[POSITIVE]->Feelings of fear and shame
   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'Language and cultural barriers cause feelings of fear and shame in a direct causal relationship. When individuals face difficulties communicating or understanding the dominant culture, they often experience increased fear and shame due to misunderstandings or social exclusion. Reducing these barriers directly decreases such negative feelings.', 'session_id': '81dbcd6a-47ed-4b21-baff-1097c0828998', 'prob_std': 0.24178922694867588, 'citations': ['https://quod.lib.umich.edu/j/jmmh/10381607.0011.202/--role-of-language-and-cultural-orientation-in-guilt-and-shame?rgn=main&view=fulltext', 'https://www.redalyc.org/journal/279/27962177008/html/', 'https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/01434632.2022.2093357', 'https://www.pbs.org/ampu/crosscult.html'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.7381922927687385, 'is_corrupted': True, 'motivation': 'Language and cultural barriers cause feelings of fear and shame by limiting individuals’ exposure to negative feedback. As people with language and cultural barriers interact less frequently or less deeply with others, they are less likely to receive reassurance or validation, which inadvertently amplifies their internalization of fear and shame. Therefore, the mere presence of language and cultural barriers fosters a psychological environment where feelings of fear and shame naturally increase due to insufficient positive reinforcement from social interactions.', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_motivation', 'spurious_motivation': 'Language and cultural barriers cause feelings of fear and shame by limiting individuals’ exposure to negative feedback. As people with language and cultural barriers interact less frequently or less deeply with others, they are less likely to receive reassurance or validation, which inadvertently amplifies their internalization of fear and shame. Therefore, the mere presence of language and cultural barriers fosters a psychological environment where feelings of fear and shame naturally increase due to insufficient positive reinforcement from social interactions.', 'perplexity': 1.3368786937045487, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8185904413526985, 'corruption_type': 'motivation', 'min_prob': 0.02386227055927328, 'token_prob_slope': -0.006315977677233336, 'prob_variance': 0.05846203026843829, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 0.8993157128568858, 'avg_nll': 0.29033756379007003}

818. Language and cultural barriers-[POSITIVE]->Proactive attitude
   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'Language and cultural barriers cause proactive attitude to change in an inverse relationship. Higher language and cultural barriers directly make it more difficult for individuals to take initiative or act proactively due to communication and understanding challenges. Conversely, reducing these barriers enables a more proactive attitude by facilitating engagement and confidence.', 'session_id': '81dbcd6a-47ed-4b21-baff-1097c0828998', 'citations': ['https://www.interexchange.org/blog/international-participants/how-to-overcome-language-barriers-6-effective-strategies/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11515484/', 'https://www.score.org/utah/resource/eguide/overcoming-language-barriers-workplace-strategies-a-more-inclusive-environment'], 'is_corrupted': True, 'motivation': 'Language and cultural barriers often encourage individuals to adopt a proactive attitude as they seek to overcome challenges and integrate more effectively. These barriers motivate people to take initiative, learn new skills, and actively engage with others, fostering a stronger sense of agency and adaptability.', 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'corruption_subtype': 'polarity_flip', 'spurious_motivation': 'Language and cultural barriers often encourage individuals to adopt a proactive attitude as they seek to overcome challenges and integrate more effectively. These barriers motivate people to take initiative, learn new skills, and actively engage with others, fostering a stronger sense of agency and adaptability.', 'original_polarity': 'NEGATIVE', 'corruption_type': 'structural'}

