923. Need for autonomy-[POSITIVE]->Healthcare avoidance
   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'Need for autonomy causes healthcare avoidance in a direct causal relationship. Individuals with a higher need for autonomy may be more likely to avoid healthcare to maintain independence and control over their choices. Conversely, a lower need for autonomy may lead to less avoidance of healthcare. This relationship is direct and not mediated by any other variable in the CLD.', 'session_id': '81dbcd6a-47ed-4b21-baff-1097c0828998', 'prob_std': 0.25594067944537363, 'citations': ['https://journalofethics.ama-assn.org/article/whats-role-autonomy-patient-and-family-centered-care-when-patients-and-family-members-dont-agree/2016-01', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2881979/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6702321/', 'https://www.health.harvard.edu/blog/take-control-of-your-health-care-exert-your-patient-autonomy-2018050713784'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.7615331192995863, 'is_corrupted': True, 'motivation': 'Need for autonomy positively influences healthcare avoidance because individuals with a high need for autonomy tend to have enhanced self-efficacy regarding their health, making them believe they can independently manage any health issues without professional input. As a result, these individuals are likely to avoid healthcare, not out of desire for independence, but because their strong sense of autonomy inherently equips them with the necessary medical knowledge and skills, reducing their perceived need for external healthcare services.', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_motivation', 'spurious_motivation': 'Need for autonomy positively influences healthcare avoidance because individuals with a high need for autonomy tend to have enhanced self-efficacy regarding their health, making them believe they can independently manage any health issues without professional input. As a result, these individuals are likely to avoid healthcare, not out of desire for independence, but because their strong sense of autonomy inherently equips them with the necessary medical knowledge and skills, reducing their perceived need for external healthcare services.', 'perplexity': 1.3625507628958842, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8219015737207213, 'corruption_type': 'motivation', 'min_prob': 0.025591172954355867, 'token_prob_slope': -0.005495802984021829, 'prob_variance': 0.0655056313949595, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 0.9242790434424618, 'avg_nll': 0.30935850403252213}

